RenderObject is responsible for the actual rendering work, such as:

Layout → deciding size and position
Painting → drawing pixels/content on the screen 
Hit testing → determining what was touched/clicked

So the three trees can be remembered like this:

Widget Tree → describes the UI structure
Element Tree → maintains the UI objects and manages/reuses them during rebuilds
RenderObject Tree → performs the actual layout, painting, and hit testing

Simple example
Text("Hello")
    ↓
Widget
    ↓
Element
    ↓
RenderObject
    ↓
Layout → where/how big?
Paint  → draw "Hello"
Interview answer in your own words

